course: dictionary
lesson: 4793
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around a word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Humanity» is a good example.
explain: «Three grains feed much of humanity: rice, wheat and maize.» Here humanity means all the people in the world, the human race. Swap in that meaning and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «She showed great humanity» is different. The word great and the feeling tell you it means kindness and care for others. Try the world meaning there and it does not fit.
fact: «Humanity» can mean all the people in the world together, the human race.
fact: «Humanity» can also mean kindness and care for others, as in «She showed great humanity».
fact: «The humanities» are school and university subjects about people and culture, such as history, languages and religious studies.
fact: In history lessons you may hear «crimes against humanity», which means terrible acts against people everywhere.
fact: A good check is to swap each meaning into the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
exercise: «Three grains feed much of humanity: rice, wheat and maize.» What does humanity mean here? | *All the people in the world | A group of school subjects | Kindness and care for others | Being very brave
exercise: «She showed great humanity.» What does humanity mean here? | All the people in the world | Being very tall | A school subject about history | *Kindness and care for others
exercise: Your timetable lists «the humanities». Which subjects might they be? | *History, languages and religious studies | Maths, science and PE | Cooking and computing | Football and drama
test: «Extreme poverty has fallen from most of humanity around 1820.» In this sentence, what does humanity mean? | *All the people in the world | A history lesson | A type of grain | Kindness and care for others
test: What does «an act of humanity» most likely mean? | A grain that feeds people | *A kind act that cares for others | A school subject about languages | A sad story about the past
exam: What is the best way to find which meaning of humanity a writer means? | *Read the words around it and swap each meaning into the sentence | Skip the word and never think about it again | Always pick the first meaning in the dictionary | Guess at random
